From b5b0bbffe5a347f0b8df339757f592fb652067db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 02:26:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: mtk-sd: propagate pinctrl errors during voltage
 switching

The voltage-switch callback discards pinctrl_select_state() errors and
returns success after setting VQMMC. If the requested pin state cannot be
applied, the MMC core therefore treats the signaling-voltage switch as
complete and may continue the transfer sequence with mismatched pad state.

Return the selected pin state's result for both 1.8 V and 3.3 V. This lets
the MMC core handle the failed transition through its existing error path.
Preserve the regulator-error and missing-supply behavior. This does not
add a driver-local regulator rollback or alter the order of operations.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 drivers/mmc/host/mtk-sd.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/mtk-sd.c b/drivers/mmc/host/mtk-sd.c
index 01ea3ad..b66b65e 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/mtk-sd.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/mtk-sd.c
@@ -1681,9 +1681,8 @@ static int msdc_ops_switch_volt(struct mmc_host *mmc, struct mmc_ios *ios)
 
 		/* Apply different pinctrl settings for different signal voltage */
 		if (ios->signal_voltage == MMC_SIGNAL_VOLTAGE_180)
-			pinctrl_select_state(host->pinctrl, host->pins_uhs);
-		else
-			pinctrl_select_state(host->pinctrl, host->pins_default);
+			return pinctrl_select_state(host->pinctrl, host->pins_uhs);
+		return pinctrl_select_state(host->pinctrl, host->pins_default);
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
